  cameraFollow: 4
  homeTitle: HOME
  homeBody: 'The shuttle drops out of the jump above the colony. Lena is waiting
    at the dock with Pip on her shoulders, Mom right behind them.


    Everyone
    is there. Everyone is well.

    Kestrel-9 is just a cold little light in the
    sky now.'
  barelyTitle: HOME, BARELY
  barelyBody: 'You made it home. The dock smells of rain and engine oil.


    {names}
    can hardly stand. The ticket ate every credit you had, and the medicine will
    have to wait a little longer.

    But you are together.'
  lateTitle: TOO LATE?
  lateBody: 'Nobody is waiting at the dock.


    A neighbour finds you: {names}
    went to the clinic three nights ago. You saved every credit for the ticket.

    The
    ticket was the easy part.'
